{
  "id": "book-18",
  "checkpoint": 2,
  "title": "The First Conversation",
  "summary": "Paul para em um pequeno café, conversa com um homem antes do trabalho e aprende que às vezes é preciso apenas dar o primeiro passo.",
  "audio_url": "/audios/book-18.mp3",
  "word_count_target": 125,
  "story_en": "Paul walks down the street and stops at a small café. He sees a man sitting near the door with a book in his hands. Paul smiles and says, “Good morning. Is this seat free?” The man looks up and smiles. “Yes, it is. Please sit down.”\n\nPaul sits at the table and asks, “Do you come here often?” The man says, “I come here every morning before work. The coffee is good, and the people are friendly.”\n\nPaul orders a coffee and a sandwich. While he waits, he tells the man about his journey. The man listens and asks, “Where are you going?” Paul points toward the street and says, “I am going forward, but I do not know exactly where I will go.”\n\nThe man smiles. “Sometimes, you just need to take the first step.”",
